WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.764 --> 00:00:14.485
by one the short winter days came and went.

2
00:00:15.826 --> 00:00:19.428
But for Pollyanna the days were long and sometimes full of pain.

3
00:00:22.569 --> 00:00:28.772
While other children went skating on the frozen ice or sledding on the snowy hills, Pollyanna lay in

4
00:00:28.832 --> 00:00:35.687
bed. Now that Aunt Polly was playing the Glad Game, Pollyanna tried to be cheerful.

5
00:00:37.448 --> 00:00:38.008
Like Mrs.

6
00:00:38.048 --> 00:00:40.470
Snow, Pollyanna had taken up knitting.

7
00:00:40.490 --> 00:00:45.193
"At least I can still use my arms and hands!"

8
00:00:45.734 --> 00:00:46.814
she said to Aunt Polly.

9
00:00:46.834 --> 00:00:52.598
"Hold out your arms, and we'll wind this yarn into a ball," Aunt Polly said.

10
00:00:58.142 --> 00:01:00.344
They had just finished when Nancy entered the room.

11
00:01:01.408 --> 00:01:04.050
"You have two visitors, Pollyanna," she said.

12
00:01:04.070 --> 00:01:06.212
"Two at once?"

13
00:01:07.553 --> 00:01:08.954
Pollyanna was delighted.

14
00:01:08.974 --> 00:01:11.156
"I rarely have one."

15
00:01:11.176 --> 00:01:15.580
"I'd better go see who they are," Aunt Polly said.

16
00:01:18.582 --> 00:01:19.903
A few minutes later, Mr.

17
00:01:19.943 --> 00:01:22.305
Pendleton and Jimmy entered Pollyanna's room.

18
00:01:23.786 --> 00:01:28.250
Mr. Pendleton was carrying another prism, and Jimmy had a box of chocolates.

19
00:01:28.270 --> 00:01:31.256
"We won't stay long," Mr.

20
00:01:31.296 --> 00:01:32.097
Pendleton said.

21
00:01:32.117 --> 00:01:35.598
"I just wanted you to know how well Jimmy's doing.

22
00:01:36.018 --> 00:01:37.679
He's turning into a fine boy!"

23
00:01:37.699 --> 00:01:43.281
"I have a wonderful home now," Jimmy added.

24
00:01:43.301 --> 00:01:47.043
"Mr. Pendleton is turning into a fine family!"

25
00:01:47.063 --> 00:01:49.984
"I owe it all to you!"

26
00:01:50.584 --> 00:01:51.284
Jimmy and Mr.

27
00:01:51.324 --> 00:01:53.645
Pendleton said to Pollyanna at the same time.

28
00:01:55.046 --> 00:01:56.546
They looked at each other and laughed.

29
00:01:58.227 --> 00:02:01.389
Noticing how happy they were together, Pollyanna smiled.

30
00:02:01.409 --> 00:02:04.250
"I'm so glad!"

31
00:02:06.971 --> 00:02:10.272
As spring arrived, there was little change in Pollyanna's condition.

32
00:02:14.334 --> 00:02:18.736
The townspeople kept up with the latest news, but everyone felt discouraged.

33
00:02:19.996 --> 00:02:20.957
Despite Dr.

34
00:02:20.997 --> 00:02:23.838
Mead's treatments, Pollyanna was not improving.

35
00:02:25.499 --> 00:02:27.960
Dr. Chilton was especially concerned about her.

36
00:02:28.736 --> 00:02:33.480
Although he never spoke to Aunt Polly, he always managed to hear about Pollyanna's condition.

37
00:02:36.743 --> 00:02:40.786
"I need to do more than worry about Pollyanna," he thought one day in his office.

38
00:02:42.648 --> 00:02:44.929
The next Saturday morning, he went to see Mr.

39
00:02:44.949 --> 00:02:51.775
Pendleton. It was a lovely spring day, and the windows were open as the two men sat in

40
00:02:51.815 --> 00:02:52.476
the library.

41
00:02:52.496 --> 00:02:56.979
"I've come to you because you've lived in this town your whole life," Dr.

42
00:02:57.019 --> 00:02:57.640
Chilton said.

43
00:02:58.644 --> 00:03:02.607
"Of anyone here, you know the most about my past relationship with Polly Harrington.

44
00:03:04.008 --> 00:03:05.289
I want to examine Pollyanna.

45
00:03:05.749 --> 00:03:06.710
I must examine her!"

46
00:03:06.730 --> 00:03:09.512
"Why can't you?"

47
00:03:11.113 --> 00:03:14.955
"You know very well that I haven't been inside that house for over 15 years.

48
00:03:16.036 --> 00:03:19.499
When Miss Polly and I quarreled, she said she'd never ask me there again.

49
00:03:20.639 --> 00:03:23.481
Not unless she was ready to beg my forgiveness and marry me."

50
00:03:25.403 --> 00:03:27.104
Mr. Pendleton thought for a moment.

51
00:03:28.444 --> 00:03:30.625
"I don't understand why you have to be asked to the house.

52
00:03:31.106 --> 00:03:32.026
Can't you go on your own?"

53
00:03:33.827 --> 00:03:35.448
Dr. Chilton shook his head.

54
00:03:35.468 --> 00:03:38.049
"Out of courtesy to Dr.

55
00:03:38.089 --> 00:03:38.830
Warren and Dr.

56
00:03:38.890 --> 00:03:40.871
Mead, I can't just barge in."

57
00:03:40.891 --> 00:03:45.394
"Maybe you need to focus on making up with Miss Polly.

58
00:03:46.574 --> 00:03:47.715
What did you quarrel about?"

59
00:03:49.216 --> 00:03:50.076
"Forget the quarrel."

60
00:03:50.977 --> 00:03:53.578
The doctor made an impatient gesture and stood up.

61
00:03:53.598 --> 00:03:56.660
"It was a silly argument about nothing.

62
00:03:57.852 --> 00:04:02.213
What's important is that if I can see Pollyanna, there's a 90 percent chance she'll walk again."

63
00:04:04.254 --> 00:04:04.734
As Dr.

64
00:04:04.774 --> 00:04:07.975
Chilton said that in a loud voice, he paced over to the window.

65
00:04:10.216 --> 00:04:12.697
In the garden below, Jimmy was pulling weeds.

66
00:04:14.097 --> 00:04:17.798
He stopped weeding and sat up, his ears wide open.

67
00:04:17.818 --> 00:04:20.179
"Pollyanna! Walk again!"

68
00:04:20.579 --> 00:04:21.879
Mr. Pendleton exclaimed.

69
00:04:22.920 --> 00:04:23.920
"What are you talking about?"

70
00:04:25.472 --> 00:04:28.594
"I have a doctor friend who specializes in this type of paralysis.

71
00:04:29.535 --> 00:04:34.478
From what I've been able to gather, Pollyanna's case sounds similar to one he just cured."

72
00:04:34.498 --> 00:04:37.600
"You must see her right away!"

73
00:04:38.280 --> 00:04:40.321
Mr. Pendleton was now standing too.

74
00:04:40.341 --> 00:04:42.322
"Couldn't you see her through Dr.

75
00:04:42.342 --> 00:04:44.424
Warren?" "No!"

76
00:04:45.204 --> 00:04:47.425
Dr. Chilton slammed his fist on Mr.

77
00:04:47.445 --> 00:04:48.266
Pendleton's desk.

78
00:04:49.106 --> 00:04:51.548
"Dr. Warren suggested early on that I examine Pollyanna.

79
00:04:52.396 --> 00:04:54.978
But Miss Polly said no so firmly that Dr.

80
00:04:54.998 --> 00:04:56.698
Warren didn't dare mention it again."

81
00:04:56.719 --> 00:04:59.460
"Miss Polly must be made to ask you!"

82
00:04:59.480 --> 00:05:01.101
"But how?

83
00:05:01.461 --> 00:05:03.702
She's too proud and angry to ask me herself."

84
00:05:05.043 --> 00:05:09.446
"Miss Polly must be made to understand how vitally important this is," Mr.

85
00:05:09.486 --> 00:05:10.266
Pendleton said.

86
00:05:10.286 --> 00:05:13.188
"And who's going to do that?"

87
00:05:13.568 --> 00:05:15.189
Dr. Chilton said bitterly.

88
00:05:17.330 --> 00:05:18.691
Mr. Pendleton groaned.

89
00:05:18.711 --> 00:05:20.572
"I have no idea."

90
00:05:22.792 --> 00:05:26.615
Outside the window Jimmy had hardly moved since he started eavesdropping.

91
00:05:26.635 --> 00:05:29.457
"I know," he whispered.

92
00:05:29.477 --> 00:05:31.298
"I'm going to do it!"

93
00:05:32.799 --> 00:05:37.562
As fast as he could, Jimmy ran down Pendleton Hill toward Miss Polly's house.
